cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "xenium-spatial-niche: permutation-based analysis of cell-state co-localisation and spatial niches in single-cell-resolution spatial transcriptomics"
abstract: >-
  R toolkit that tests whether labelled cell populations are found in each
  other's local neighbourhoods more often than tissue architecture alone would
  predict, using within-compartment permutation nulls restricted to connected
  tissue components and the section as the unit of inference. Modules cover
  tissue geometry QC, co-localisation, distance decay, depth-stratified
  exposure contrasts and neighbourhood-associated genes with a segmentation
  spillover filter.
authors:
